    "body": "View of the mill at Canadian Malartic. Credit: Agnico Eagle Mines.\nBy: Northern Miner Staff November 18, 2026\nAgnico Eagle Mines (TSX, NYSE: AEM) heads into its capital markets day Wednesday with a goal of producing more than 4 million oz. of gold a year in the early 2030s and a nearer-term test in Quebec, where it must bring more underground ore to surface as mining winds down in the Canadian Malartic pit complex. The company expects this year’s production near the bottom of its 3.3-million to 3.5-million-oz. range after ground movement forced it to revise the mining plan at the Barnat pit. Agnico has identified 2030 as the first year of a bigger increase in group output. Its investor webcast is scheduled for 10:30 a.m. Toronto time. “Most of our peers will do 30 or 40% detailed engineering before they announce a project,” CEO Ammar Al-Joundi said at a Toronto symposium on Nov. 9. Agnico is prepared to spend more on engineering before committing to construction to reduce the risk of cost overruns, he said.\nUnderground push\nAt Canadian Malartic, the question is how quickly underground development can replace lost open-pit tonnes and fill the mill. The Barnat ground movement could cost Agnico up to 150,000 oz. in each of 2027 and 2028, the company said in its third-quarter results.\nThe Odyssey underground operation mined a record 391,000 tonnes in the third quarter. East Gouldie, one of its deposits, produced 27,250 oz. Agnico has said further investments could help bring Canadian Malartic’s annual production towards 1 million oz. as early as 2033. Nunavut’s Hope Bay provides a measure of what the next ounces could cost. Agnico approved the project in May at an estimated initial cost of $2.4 billion (C$3.4 billion). Production could begin as early as 2030 and average 435,000 oz. a year once the operation reaches a steady rate, the company said in its investment decision. Agnico shares closed C$3.20 stronger at C$247.49 in Toronto on Tuesday. They have traded between C$188.48 and C$348.94 over the past year.\nPrint\nTAG: gold gold exploration gold mines gold mining gold production gold projects\nCOMMODITY: Gold\nREGION: Canada\nCOMPANY: Agnico Eagle Agnico Eagle Mines\nRepublish this article",
